<title>USA: Seidman named to head US Thrift Supervision office.</title>
<headline>Seidman named to head US Thrift Supervision office.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHBROOK, Ill. 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House said on Wednesday President Bill Clinton intended to nominate White House aide Ellen Seidman to be director of the U.S. Treasury Department's Office of Thrift Supervision.</p>
<p>In a statement released in Illinois, where Clinton is on a one-day trip to speak on education, the White House said that Seidman is currently special assistant to the president for economic policy on the National Economic Council.</p>
